 G←EstablishSecrets G
⍝ Establishes from the INI file what crash reports and the start-up report leave out or mask:
⍝ * `G.SecretHeaders`: the headers of `SecretHeaders` plus those of `[TRAP]MaskHeaders`
⍝ * `G.SecretQueryParms`: the query parameters of `SecretQueryParms` plus those of `[TRAP]MaskQueryParms`
⍝ * `G.SaveRequestBody`: `[TRAP]SaveRequestBody`, default 0: a crash report does not keep request bodies
⍝ * `G.SecretIniKeys`: the parts of key names of `SecretIniKeys` plus those of `[LOGGING]MaskIniKeys`
⍝ See `SaveCrashRequest` and `CollectStartParms`.
 G.SecretHeaders←∪SecretHeaders,GetNameList'TRAP:MaskHeaders'
 G.SecretQueryParms←∪SecretQueryParms,GetNameList'TRAP:MaskQueryParms'
 G.SecretIniKeys←∪SecretIniKeys,GetNameList'LOGGING:MaskIniKeys'
 G.SaveRequestBody←0 G.INI.Get'TRAP:SaveRequestBody'
 'Invalid: value of "SaveRequestBody" in INI file'⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨~(⊂G.SaveRequestBody)∊0 1
